# Extra packages for the 64-bit ISO only (added to the list in "packages").
# Newer laptops and Chromebooks (with MrChromebox's UEFI firmware) need more
# for sound than old netbooks: the sound chip's own firmware (Intel/AMD SOF),
# speaker amplifier firmware, and "UCM" profiles that say how the speakers
# and headphone jack are wired. PipeWire uses those profiles; plain ALSA
# can't, which is why these machines had no sound at all.
sof-firmware linux-firmware-intel linux-firmware-cirrus
alsa-ucm-conf
pipewire pipewire-alsa pipewire-pulse wireplumber
# Chromebook keyboards: the top row (back, refresh, brightness, volume...)
# and Search+arrows for Page Up/Down, Home/End (cherrystone-chromebook-keys)
keyd keyd-openrc
